I split the string by dots into three integer fields, then update them according to which part is named. The patch goes up by one, and done. The minor goes up and the patch is set to zero. The major goes up and both minor and patch are set to zero. Since the version strings in the examples show no prefixes, I take the input literally and convert it with the ordinary reader. If the string were malformed, a list with fewer or more than three items would come out of the split, but the spec gives only Example versions so inputs are guaranteed to be well formed.

