                duration = t - parked[car]
                fees[car] = duration * rate
                del parked[car]
    return fees
```

From each enter or exit event record, the function must build a dictionary of fees: every car that exits successfully receives an entry mapped to (exit time minus entry time) times the given rate.

The approach is to iterate through the events while keeping a dictionary of parked cars and their arrival times.

For an enter event, I ignore the record if that car is already in the parked dictionary. If it is not, I store its arrival time there. For an exit event, I only take a fee and remove the car if it is currently parked, so I check whether the car has an entry and its exit time is greater than or equal to its arrival time. Only in that case do I compute the fee and remove the car. Each fee is recorded under the car's ID in the result dictionary, which is returned after the loop. Arrivals are not paid for, nor are exits for cars that left or never entered.

