Visiting in this sequence implies marking cells as they are added, so I keep four frame counters: the leftmost column, the rightmost column, the top row, and the bottom row. At the start, those edges all include the top-left corner. Each visit performs one of the four scan sorts with the operating edges: left-to-right across the top, top-to-bottom down the right, right-to-left across the bottom, and bottom-to-top up the left. After each scan, the corresponding edge moves inward. The loop repeats as long as the top row is above or equal to the bottom row and the leftmost column is to the left or equal to the rightmost column. Every cell is visited exactly once because each scan moves a boundary inward by one cell.

